    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d875">

                <pb facs="1116" n="1014" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg1014"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">681.003/161: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-03-08T19:00:00-05:00">March 8, 1935—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>48. Your 96, March 6, noon. You may advise British orally that this Government is
                    now negotiating with the Spanish Government <pb facs="1117" n="1015"
                        xml:id="pg1015"/> with the view of obtaining settlement of certain claims of
                    American proteges arising in the Spanish Zone of Morocco, in exchange for formal
                    recognition of the Spanish Protectorate by the United States. While the Spanish
                    have indicated they desire to inject the question of surrender of
                    extraterritorial rights into negotiations, the American negotiators have been
                    instructed by the Department to make it clear to the Spanish that we desire to
                    limit the present negotiations to a settlement of claims in exchange for formal
                    recognition. This Government has no present intention of giving up its
                    extraterritorial privileges.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
